WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.596
Lesson six.

00:00:01.596 --> 00:00:06.423
Now we watch the real training run, one generation at a time.

00:00:07.023 --> 00:00:09.479
First, how do we score a genome?

00:00:09.479 --> 00:00:13.462
Its fitness is the average reward over five flights.

00:00:14.062 --> 00:00:20.483
Every genome in a generation flies the same starting positions, so the comparison is fair.

00:00:20.483 --> 00:00:26.352
The starting positions change each generation, so no genome can memorise one.

00:00:26.952 --> 00:00:31.538
But five flights are noisy, and the top genome is often just lucky.

00:00:31.538 --> 00:00:37.715
So each generation, its champion also flies a hundred flights that no genome ever trained on.

00:00:37.715 --> 00:00:43.213
We only call the problem solved when that unseen average reaches two hundred.

00:00:43.813 --> 00:00:47.775
Every dot is one genome, and its color shows its species.

00:00:47.775 --> 00:00:54.602
In generation zero, every network is just the inputs wired straight to the outputs, with random weights.

00:00:54.602 --> 00:00:56.913
Almost all of them crash.

00:00:57.513 --> 00:01:01.553
Generation by generation, the cloud of dots creeps upward.

00:01:01.553 --> 00:01:03.573
Notice how wide it stays.

00:01:03.573 --> 00:01:10.117
Mutation keeps producing bad genomes too, and that variety is what evolution searches through.

00:01:10.717 --> 00:01:14.531
The green line is the champion on the hundred unseen flights.

00:01:14.531 --> 00:01:18.014
It first passes two hundred in generation thirty-seven.

00:01:18.014 --> 00:01:22.104
The best champion came from generation one hundred and sixty-four.

00:01:22.104 --> 00:01:26.692
On another hundred fresh flights, it lands ninety-five percent of the time.

00:01:26.692 --> 00:01:31.967
Late in the run the line sags, as the networks grow bigger without getting better.

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:36.041
Here is one whole generation flying together.

00:01:36.041 --> 00:01:41.677
All 150 genomes start from the same spot, and each flight is drawn as a trail.

00:01:41.677 --> 00:01:44.074
This is generation zero.

00:01:44.674 --> 00:01:50.251
At first, nearly every flight ends in a crash, or drifts off the screen.

00:01:51.274 --> 00:01:56.798
Fifty generations in, a few dozen trails curve down onto the pad.

00:01:57.874 --> 00:02:05.709
And late in the run, about a third of the population lands from this start, and their trails bundle together into one shared path.

00:02:05.709 --> 00:02:07.356
The rest still crash.

00:02:07.356 --> 00:02:11.914
Mutation keeps breaking things, and that is the price of searching.

00:02:12.514 --> 00:02:18.665
Finally, here are the champions from different generations, all flying the same start.

00:02:19.265 --> 00:02:21.989
The early ones crash or drift away.

00:02:21.989 --> 00:02:27.167
Later champions slow down, straighten up, and land between the flags.
